---
title: What GGE Command does
description: GGE Command plays Goodgame Empire for you while you are away. See what a bot does, what each part of the app is for, and where to start.
---

Can't be online all day? Your castles can keep working anyway. GGE Command runs a bot that signs in to Goodgame Empire as you and does the jobs you pick.

{% terms_on_page /%}

## What GGE Command is {% #what-it-is %}

GGE Command is a website. You add your {% term id="game-account" %}game account{% /term %}, choose what the bot should do, and press {% ui key="common:action.start" /%}. The bot does not run on your phone or computer. It runs on GGE Command, so it keeps working when you close the browser.

You can check on it from any browser. Each move the bot makes goes into the {% term id="log" %}logs{% /term %}, so you can read what happened while you were away.

## What your bot does while you are away {% #while-away %}

Each job is a {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %}. You switch on the plugins you want, and the bot does each one on its own. Here is some of what the bot can do today:

- Attack {% term id="robber-baron" %}Robber Baron{% /term %} castles, {% term id="fortress" %}fortresses{% /term %}, {% term id="nomad" %}Nomad{% /term %} and {% term id="samurai" %}Samurai{% /term %} camps, {% term id="khan-camp" %}Khan camps{% /term %}, {% term id="storm-islands" %}Storm Islands{% /term %} fortresses and the camps of invasion events.
- Keep {% term id="tool" %}siege tools{% /term %} and troops in stock. It buys tools from the armourer, builds tools in your workshops and recruits troops.
- Do the daily chores. It claims the login bonus, sends the tax collector out and asks your alliance for help.
- Spin the wheels with the tickets you hold, start feasts and sell loose equipment from storage.
- Move the troops out of a castle before another player's attack lands on it.
- Post attacks and event news to Discord channels, and copy your alliance chat to a Discord channel.

The full list is on the [modules overview](/modules/).

## The main parts of the app {% #main-areas %}

The app has three kinds of pages.

1. **Your war room.** The {% ui key="client:nav.overview" /%} page lists your game accounts and how each bot is doing. The {% ui key="client:nav.logs" /%} page shows every move live. The bell and your emails tell you when a bot stops and needs you. {% ui key="common:nav.settings" /%} holds your password, email and data.
2. **Modules.** Each {% term id="module" %}module{% /term %} is one page in the sidebar, grouped the same way as these docs. Pick an account at the top of the page, switch the plugins on and change their settings.
3. **Discord alerts.** Three modules connect your game to Discord. They post attacks, keep event messages up to date, and pass alliance chat both ways.

## Who it is for {% #who-its-for %}

GGE Command is for players who want their account to keep growing when they can't play. It helps most with the work that repeats every day: event attacks, chores, and keeping tools and troops stocked.

It is also for players who accept a risk. Using a bot is against the game's rules, and a game account can be banned. Read [Playing it safe](/playing-it-safe/) before you start.

## Where to start {% #start %}

1. Follow the [quick start](/quick-start/) to create your account, add a game account and start your first bot.
2. Read [How your bot runs](/how-your-bot-runs/) to learn what each status means and how {% term id="run-schedule" %}run schedules{% /term %} work.
3. Read [Playing it safe](/playing-it-safe/) for habits that keep you in control.

